 "id": "story-3-status-request",
 "name": "Story 3: a manager asks for an update",
 "description": "One of my managers asks me for an update, assuming I already have the context. Today I don't: I re-read tickets, docs and Slack threads to reconstruct it before I can give a small update. With a status page the analyst keeps current, the update is already prepared. Around that core are the loops that decide whether it stays that way: the page is refreshed faster when owners keep their sources up; nudges keep them up until they wear out the team's patience. Accurate, quick answers build my manager's confidence and they ask less; wrong answers and surprises (blocked projects they found before me) send them checking in more. Time unit: a working hour; horizon 26 weeks.",
 "time_unit": "working hour",
